.venv/
.cache/
secrets/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
captures/
oak_camera/crash_dumps/
*.mp4
*.npy
*.onnx
# ...except the face detector's own model, which is not a downloaded
# experiment but the thing yunet.py loads on every rover. deploy/manifest.json
# has always listed face_tracking/*.onnx among the daemon's sources, and with
# this rule in the way that pattern could never match anything: the model only
# reached the Banana Pi because somebody copied it by hand, and the Jetson got
# a deployed face detector that answered every count_faces with a missing file.
# 230 KB, and the alternative is a host that is one forgotten scp from blind.
!face_tracking/face_detection_yunet.onnx
calibration_backup_*.json
omni_bench/runs/

# lidar_slam/ is compiled per-machine on the board that runs it -- aarch64 now,
# armv6 before that; a committed binary could only ever be for the wrong one.
lidar_slam/libslam2d.so
lidar_slam/selftest
*.pgm

# Measured on a particular rover by driving it -- the gyro's scale and the
# wheels' counts per metre. Belongs to the machine, not the repository, and
# lives beside ~/ugv so no deploy can overwrite it. See ros_nav/calibrate_chassis.py.
odometry.json

# netprobe writes its record of what the rover looked like from a desk here.
# It is evidence about one afternoon on one network, not source.
netwatch/*.log

# ros_nav/behaviors/ is the ROS stack's one compiled component. Its build tree
# and install prefix are made on the rover by build.sh, which the manifest runs
# on every deploy; the deployer only ever copies files git tracks, so keeping
# these out is what stops a workstation build being shipped to the rover.
ros_nav/behaviors/build/
ros_nav/behaviors/build.log
ros_nav/behaviors/install/
